description: Erasezo project context — read before any edit
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the workspace root first. It carries the rules that are not
visible from the code, and most of them fail silently when broken.

The short version:

- Three folders. `erasezo-web/` is the server and site. `Erasezo-extension/` is
  the extension and is where you edit. `1.1.2_0/` is a mirror — never edit it.
- After any extension change: `npm --prefix erasezo-web run sync`
- Tests: `npm --prefix erasezo-web test` (14 suites, no real database)
- Never hardcode a colour — everything comes from `public/tokens.css`.
- Never hardcode a price — the site reads `/api/plans`.
- Don't add a dependency, or a control that doesn't do anything.
